message-queue-linker declared nine host languages and consumes NOTHING. Its
entry point is link_message_queues(root: Path): it takes the repository root,
scans the tree itself, and mints BOTH ENDS of every edge, so no pass supplies
its source and none supplies its destination. Its clause is now empty. The old
comment stated the WI-rasal diagnosis without noticing -- "clients exist across
all common backend languages" is a statement about the world, where depends_on
is the passes whose OUTPUT this pass reads.

THAT COLLIDED WITH A RATIFIED CRITERION, and the criterion was amended rather
than the declaration falsified. WI-dilab's closure criterion (INV-hujog's gate)
requires every Bridge/Framework/Protocol linker to declare a non-empty
depends_on, and message-queue-linker is a Protocol linker. The criterion's
premise -- that such a linker always reads some analyzer's output -- is false
for a self-scanner, and forcing a non-empty clause does not make the declaration
true, it makes it a list of passes the linker never reads: the too-wide,
false-all-clear shape WI-ditir and WI-zujan exist to remove. Owner was shown the
collision and ruled the amendment.

The allowance is narrow and POSITIVE: the module docstring must state, in a
fixed phrase the gate greps for, why the clause is empty. SILENCE PLUS AN EMPTY
CLAUSE IS STILL AN OFFENCE, because silence cannot be told from having forgotten
to declare, which is the case the criterion exists to catch. Two further tests
keep the exception honest -- one asserts the branch is actually exercised (a
dead allowance should be deleted, not carried), one asserts an undeclared empty
clause still trips the gate.

SIX OF EIGHT REMAIN, deliberately. http-linker (13 declared), subprocess-linker
(9, scans only **/*.py), orm-linker (8, scans only **/*.py), grpc-linker (12,
and it reads ctx.edges), event-sourcing-linker (6) and crypto-flow-linker (10)
all genuinely read ctx.symbols, so part of each clause may name a real producer
and each needs its own derivation. http-linker's is hardest: route_of accepts
both an analyzer-written framework_role == "route" marker and a framework-YAML
concept == "route" entry, so its producer set is not analyzer-only.

